// Design 257 §1, the check that comes with the adoption: a platform slot
// range-checks the FOLDED value, so a fold that goes negative into a `UInt` is
// the same clean "does not fit" a bare negative literal gives — never a
// silent reinterpretation of the bits.
//
// The signed-domain gotcha at the fixed widths is unchanged and lives in
// `const_expression_signed_domain_error.saw` (`1 << 63` is `Int.min`, so it
// does not fit a `UInt64`); this is the platform pair's own row.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: constant expression -2 does not fit in `UInt`

static NEG: UInt = 3 - 5

func main() {
    print("{}", NEG)
}
